# Append-only logs: use git's built-in `union` merge driver so two PRs that
# each append a new entry at end-of-file merge by KEEPING BOTH sides instead of
# producing a conflict. `docs/03-decision-log.md` is append-only (see CLAUDE.md
# "Edits to design documents"), and every PR adds a `D-progress-N` entry at the
# tail, so concurrent PRs collided there constantly and each had to rebase +
# renumber + re-run the full (multi-hour) CI, which fast-moving `main` then
# out-churned. `union` is a built-in driver GitHub honors on its own merges, so
# the append stops being a conflict. Note: it does not renumber, so two entries
# can share a `D-progress-N` number after an auto-merge — that is cosmetic
# (numbers are not load-bearing); reconcile opportunistically or via a lint.
docs/03-decision-log.md merge=union
